# ==============================================================================
# NoteIn Web - Google Identity Services & Google Drive / Picker API Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# Follow these steps to obtain credentials from Google Cloud Console:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project or select an existing project.
# 3. Enable Required APIs (APIs & Services > Library):
#    - Google Drive API (https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/drive.googleapis.com)
#    - Google Picker API (https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/picker.googleapis.com)
# 4. Configure OAuth Consent Screen (APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen):
#    - User Type: External (or Internal if using Google Workspace)
#    - App name: NoteIn Web
#    - User support email: your email
#    - Scopes: add "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file" (per-file access for Picker)
#    - Test users: Add your Google account email while in Testing mode.
# 5. Create OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID (APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID):
#    - Application type: Web application
#    - Name: NoteIn Web Client
#    - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        http://localhost:5173
#        http://localhost:5174
#        https://your-production-domain.com
#    - Authorized redirect URIs: (none required for GIS popup / token client flow)
# 6. Create API Key for Google Picker (APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > API Key):
#    - Restrict key:
#        - API restrictions: Restrict to "Google Picker API" and "Google Drive API"
#        - Application restrictions: HTTP referrers (e.g., http://localhost:5173/*, http://localhost:5174/*)
# 7. Copy your Project Number (from Google Cloud Project Settings) for VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values:
# cp .env.example .env.local
# ==============================================================================

# OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID (Format: <project-number>-<hash>.apps.googleusercontent.com)
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Google Cloud API Key with Google Picker API & Google Drive API enabled
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Google Cloud Project Number (numeric ID shown on Google Cloud Dashboard / Project Settings)
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
